  "surface_derivation": "Complete original published per-label binary masks; Lewiner marching cubes at 0.5; exact source sform applied. No padding, smoothing, cleanup, component deletion, decimation, capping, relabeling, fitting or mesh repair.",
  "source_annotation_workflow": "Original paper S3 reports heart-subpart model training from arterial CT labels transferred to aligned native CT images, then prediction in all CT sequences. Main paper reports all final dataset annotations manually reviewed and corrected when necessary. Per-interface independent expert accuracy is not supplied.",
  "source_label_meanings": "Original label filenames remain unchanged. Published TotalSegmentator cardiac methods describe the output as LV myocardium and four cardiac chamber volumes (DOI 10.1038/s41467-024-46977-3). This supports LV myocardial context, not global myocardium or RV/atrial walls. Chamber-region masks provide separate volume labels; exact cavity/appendage/valve-plane interface conventions and per-interface anatomical accuracy remain unverified. No new wall is inferred from any chamber label.",
